          "text": "The **crucible:debater** agent (running on Claude Sonnet) is responsible for generating proposals. Here's how it works:\n\n### Agents involved in proposals\n\n| Agent | Model | Role |\n|-------|-------|------|\n| **crucible:debater** | Sonnet | Proposes solutions, attacks, and defends |\n| **crucible:arbiter** | Opus | Synthesizes final verdict from all proposals |\n\n### Proposal flow\n\n1. **Round 1 (PROPOSE)** — Each debater agent independently proposes a complete solution. All run in parallel (2–5 agents depending on the `--agents` flag), named Alpha, Beta, Gamma, etc.\n2. **Round 2 (CRITIQUE)** — Agents attack each other's proposals\n3. **Round 2 (DEFEND)** — Agents refine their proposals against critiques\n4. **Convergence check** — If agents still disagree, a Round 3 repeats attack/defend\n5. **Arbiter** — Reviews all proposals and defenses, scores agents, and synthesizes the final answer\n\n### Key files\n\n- `agents/debater.md` — The debater agent prompt (handles PROPOSE/CRITIQUE/DEFEND modes)\n- `agents/arbiter.md` — The arbiter agent prompt\n- `commands/crucible.md` — Orchestrator that coordinates the rounds",
